  "summary_en": "North Dakota statute regulating law-enforcement surveillance by unmanned aerial vehicles and autonomous robots. It requires warrants with data collection statements, limits admissibility of evidence, bans armed drones and autonomous lethal or less-lethal force, sets exceptions, and imposes documentation and data retention rules.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Data from UAVs or robots is inadmissible unless obtained under a warrant or a warrant exception.",
   "Warrants must include a data collection statement covering authorizers, locations, duration, and data handling.",
   "Law enforcement may not use UAVs armed with lethal weapons; robot lethal force must be remote-controlled and cannot activate autonomously.",
   "Agencies must adopt a use-of-force policy for UAVs and robots before authorizing force.",
   "Flight information is kept five years; non-evidentiary data is kept at most ninety days."
  ],
